# Vulnerabilities we have consciously accepted, each with an EXPIRY DATE.
#
# An ignore with no end date is not a decision, it is a vulnerability somebody stopped looking
# at. Trivy re-reports an entry once its date passes, which forces the question to be asked
# again rather than quietly inherited by whoever maintains this next.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#   # why it is accepted, and what would change that
#
# (empty — nothing accepted yet)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vendored Go modules inside the FrankenPHP binary itself (usr/local/bin/frankenphp).
#
# These cannot be fixed from this repository: they are compiled into the upstream binary, and
# the only fix is a FrankenPHP release built against newer modules. The Debian packages this
# image inherits ARE fixed, at build time, by the apt-get upgrade in docker/frankenphp/
# Dockerfile — these four are the remainder that no amount of patching here can reach.
#
# kin-openapi and grpc are used by Caddy's admin and config-validation paths. This image does
# not expose the Caddy admin endpoint, so they are not reachable from the request path — but
# "not reachable today" is a property of the current config, which is exactly why these expire
# rather than being accepted permanently.
#
# On expiry: check whether a newer dunglas/frankenphp:php8.5 has shipped, and drop whichever
# of these it fixes.
GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw exp:2026-11-22
CVE-2026-76905 exp:2026-11-22
CVE-2026-77354 exp:2026-11-22
